    "question_text": "At the sea level, the dry air mass percentage composition is given as nitrogen gas : 70.0, oxygen gas : 27.0 and argon gas : 3.0. If total pressure is 1.15 atm , then calculate the ratio of followings respectively :<br />(i) partial pressure of nitrogen gas to partial pressure of oxygen gas<br />(ii) partial pressure of oxygen gas to partial pressure of argon gas<br />(Given : Molar mass of $\\mathrm{N}, \\mathrm{O}$ and Ar are 14, 16, and $40 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$ respectively)",
