    "correct_answer": "u0kKQ",
    "solution_text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{N}_2}}{\\mathrm{Po}_2}=\\frac{\\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{N}_2} \\cdot \\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{T}}}{\\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{O}_2} \\cdot \\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{T}}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{N}_2}}{\\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{O}_2}}$ {using Dalton's law of partial pressure}<br />$\\begin{aligned} & =\\frac{70 / 28}{27 / 32}=2.96 \\\\ & \\frac{\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{O}_2}}{\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{Ar}}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{O}_2}}{\\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{Ar}}}=\\frac{27 / 32}{3 / 40}=11.25\\end{aligned}$",
